  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{\\sqrt{3}/3}^{\\infty }\\frac{8}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "First, let's recall the following result:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{arctan}\u2061x+C\n$$\n\nWe proceed by setting the upper bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to \\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{3}/3}^{\\infty }\\frac{8}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =8\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{\\sqrt{3}/3}^{a}\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =8\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }\\operatorname{arctan}\u2061x\\,{|}_{\\sqrt{3}/3}^{a} \\\\  & =8\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }(\\operatorname{arctan}\u2061(a)-\\operatorname{arctan}\u2061(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3})) \\\\  & =8\\cdot ({lim}_{a\\to \\infty }\\operatorname{arctan}\u2061(a)-\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall the end behavior of the function $y=\\operatorname{arctan}\u2061x,$ shown in the graph below:\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\operatorname{arctan}\u2061x=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\operatorname{arctan}\u2061x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039465/assets/28afd0a065525cd225377165c2164a1ecc254b1be8aba60d64324d14430c3be4.png)\n\nUsing this to evaluate our integral, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{3}/3}^{\\infty }\\frac{8}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =8\\cdot ({lim}_{a\\to \\infty }\\operatorname{arctan}\u2061(a)-\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =8\\cdot (\\frac{\\pi }{2}-\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =8\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{8\\pi }{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
